---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import EnvValidator from '../../components/EnvValidator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title=".env File Validator"
  description="Check your .env file for duplicate keys, missing values, spaces in keys, and other common mistakes — instantly, in your browser."
>
  <EnvValidator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Common .env mistakes this catches</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Duplicate keys, where the second value silently overrides the first</li>
    <li>Spaces inside keys (invalid — most tools will fail to parse these)</li>
    <li>Empty values that might indicate a forgotten secret</li>
    <li>Lines missing the required <code>=</code> separator</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Is this safe for real secrets?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes — this tool runs entirely in your browser using client-side
    JavaScript. Nothing you paste is sent to a server or logged anywhere.
    That said, as a general practice, avoid pasting production secrets into
    any web tool when a local script would do.
  </p>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why does a duplicate key matter?</strong> Most .env parsers keep
    the last occurrence of a key and silently discard earlier ones — this
    can cause confusing bugs where a value you set earlier in the file
    doesn't take effect.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
